- Introduction to EC2
Secure, resizable compute capacity in the cloud
Like a VM, only hosted in AWS instead of your own data center
Designed to make web-scale cloud computing easier for developers
The capacity you want when you need it 
You are in complete control of your instances

Game Changer - AWS led a big change in the industry by introducing EC2
Pay only for what you use - EC2 changed the economics of computing
No wasted Capacity - Select the capacity you need right now. Grow and shrink when you need 

- EC2 Pricing 
On Demand - Pay the hour or the second, depending on the type of instance you run
Reserved - Reserved capacity for 1 to 3 years. Up to 72% discount on the hourly charge
Spot - Purchase unused capcity at a discount of up to 90%. Prices fluctuates with supply and demand
Dedicated - A physical EC2 server dedicated for your use. The most expensive option

Where to use On Demand Instances -
Flexibily - Low cost and flexibility of EC2 without any upfront pyment or long-term commitment.
Short-Term - Applications with short-term, spiky, or unpredictable workloads that cannot be interrupted
Testing the Water - Applications being developed or tested on EC2 for the first time 

Where to use Reserved Instances -
Predictable Usage - Applications with steady state or predictable usage
Specific Capcity requirements - Applications that require reserved capacity
Pay up front - You can make upfront payments to reduce the total computing costs even further
Standard RI - Up to 72% off the on-demand price
Convertible RI - Up to 54% off on-demand price. Has the option to change to a different RI type of equal or greater value
Scheduled RI - Launch within the time window you define. Match your capacity reservation to a predictable recurring schedule that only requires a fraction of a day, week or month
NOTE that it operates at regional level 
Savings plan with RI -
Save up to 72% - All AWS compute usage, regardless of instance type or a Region
Commit to 1 to 3 years - Commit to a specific amount of compute power(measured by the hour) for a 1 year or 3 year period
Super Flexible - Not only EC2, this also includes serverless technologies like lambda and Fargate

Where to use Spot Instances -
Flexibility - Applications that have flexible start and end times. Not used for websites
Cost Sensitive - Applications that are only feasible at very low compute prices
Urgent Capacity - Users with an urgent need for large amount of additional computing capacity
Use case examples - Image rendering, Geonomic sequencing, Algorithmic trading engines

When to use Dedicated Host Instances -
Compliance - Regulatory requirements that may not support multi-tenant virtualization
License - Great for licensing that does not support multi-tenancy or cloud deployments
On-Demand - Can be purchased on demand (hourly)
Reserved - Can be purchased as a reservation for up to 70% off the on-demand price

